evidence.text:
Fixture for1.ddd page P1: `body: QueryView { of: Item.all, data: rows => For { each: rows, r => Text { r.name } } }` (`ddd parse` 0 errors).
- REACT out-for1/web/src/pages/p1.tsx:20-25 —
    { itemAll.data && itemAll.data.items.length > 0 && (
      {itemAll.data.items.map((r, rIdx) => (
        <Fragment key={rIdx}>...
      ))}
    ) }
  The `{...}` sits in an EXPRESSION position (after `&& (`), so it parses as an object literal with an invalid property → SyntaxError; the file never compiles.
- FELIZ out-for1-feliz/web/src/App.fs:172-175 — `let p1View ... = (View.remoteList ... (fun allItems ->\n    yield! allItems |> List.map (fun r -> Html.p [...])))`. `yield!` is only legal inside a list/array/sequence expression; a bare lambda body is not one → F#/Fable parse error.
- FLUTTER out-for1-flutter/web/lib/pages/p1_page.dart:14 — `data: (itemAll) => itemAll.items.isEmpty ? const SizedBox.shrink() : ...itemAll.items.map((r) => Text('${r.name}'))`. `...` is only legal inside a collection literal → Dart parse error.
- vue (out-for1-vue/web/src/pages/p1.vue:21) / svelte / angular are fine (template syntax carries no such constraint).
ROOT: the three `renderForEach` seams return a CHILDREN-position-only form — src/generator/react/walker/tsx-target.ts:337ff (brace-wrapped), src/generator/feliz/feliz-target.ts:392 (`yield! ${coll} |> List.map ...`), src/generator/flutter/flutter-target.ts:438 (`...${coll}.map(...)`) — while emitQueryView (src/generator/_walker/primitives/controls.ts ~450-520) places the data-lambda body in a single-expression slot with no wrapper.

