SSE realtime wire + LiveView realtime in ONE elixir system — SOUND, both wires emitted and non-conflicting. scratchpad/elixir-audit/sse-live.ddd: out-sse2/d/lib/d_web/controllers/realtime_controller.ex subscribes to `Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(D.PubSub, "events")`, sends `text/event-stream` + `x-accel-buffering: no`, frames `%D.Orders.Events.OrderPlaced{}` as `event: OrderPlaced
data: {…,"type":"OrderPlaced"}

`, keep-alives every 15s, and ends the loop on a `chunk/2` error; independently every LiveView page subscribes to the SAME topic (`order_list_live.ex:7`, `order_detail_live.ex:7`, `order_new_live.ex:7`, `home_live.ex:7` — `if connected?(socket), do: Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(D.PubSub, "events")`) with a matching `handle_info(%D.Orders.Events.OrderPlaced{} = e, socket)` clause plus a `handle_info(_msg, socket)` catch-all. One broadcast feeds both, as the emitter's header claims. (The toast message inside those handle_info bodies is the ELX-ESCAPE-FUNNEL finding; the wiring itself is correct.)
